      "value": "Okay, so after a little bit of trial and error and lots of hours wasted on Tupper's YT video showing that there is *actually* already a way to revert to having dedicated gesture toggle buttons.\nThe video is at https://youtu.be/FKRuJl-mvmU\nYou gotta make sure that (like shown at 0:59 in his video) when reverting to the default bindings, the default bindings are actually dated August 2020. Once you activate that binding, double check to make sure that the left B button is actually bound to \"Left Quick Menu\" and NOT \"Left Application Menu Button\" or similar. If you are sure that you selected the correct binding when reverting to the defaults, good luck figuring out what the problem is. What helped for me was a full SteamVR reinstallation (yes, you *have* to remove the SteamVR folder in your steam library and the folder in AppData (%appdata%\\..\\local\\) *before* you install SteamVR again.\nOnce you made sure that your Left B button is actually bound to \"Left Quick Menu\", you can proceed to manually restore your custom bindings configuration (no, activating the old binding you used back then does not work anymore, I suggest just deleting those) and binding one or more buttons of your choice to \"Left Gesture Toggle\" and \"Right Gesture Toggle\". Do make sure that if you want to bind Gesture Toggle buttons to any of the not-actual-buttons (like the trackpad or the grip button (hey weirdo)), you do so using an actual \"button\" on that part of the controller and then select activation through force and not through touch in the configuration of the button.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
